1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,012
Carbon moves around the Earth in the carbon cycle. Plants take in carbon dioxide for photosynthesis.

2
00:00:06,012 --> 00:00:07,857
Animals get carbon by feeding.

3
00:00:07,857 --> 00:00:14,285
All living things release carbon dioxide by respiration, and decomposers release carbon from dead organisms.

4
00:00:15,345 --> 00:00:19,214
Some dead organisms weren't decomposed, and became fossil fuels.

5
00:00:19,214 --> 00:00:22,547
Burning them, called combustion, releases their carbon.

6
00:00:22,547 --> 00:00:25,999
Humans now add carbon faster than the cycle can remove it.
